id: pm-88mo8m
title: "GH-1007: assurance gate declarations omit trigger and escape the typed refusal contract"
description: "The assurance SDK accepts a structurally incomplete gate far enough to dereference trigger.length, so CLI and MCP callers receive a raw V8 TypeError instead of a stable declaration-validation refusal. Fix the SDK declaration boundary first and keep every transport aligned."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: "area:cli","area:sdk",assurance,contracts,recovery,regression
created_at: "2026-08-14T06:11:30.658Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-14T07:56:46.797Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-14T07:56:06.054Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-14T07:56:06.054Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: The public SDK declaration validator rejects a missing gate.trigger with a stable typed error naming gate.trigger; CLI and MCP normalize the same SDK error into the documented usage refusal without a raw TypeError; Missing and invalid trigger cases enumerate the same supported vocabulary; Focused unit integration and temporary packed-consumer tests exercise the exact omission path; Sentry classifies the refusal as expected usage rather than an unclassified runtime fault
parent: pm-1jzupz
risk: high
confidence: 98
reporter: GitHub issue #1007
severity: high
resolution: fixed
expected_result: Missing gate.trigger is rejected before persistence with a stable typed refusal naming the field and supported trigger vocabulary.
actual_result: The command dereferences an absent trigger and emits Cannot read properties of undefined reading length.
affected_version: 2026.8.14
regression: true
customer_impact: Agents cannot distinguish a correctable declaration error from corruption or a product crash.
